{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789777107,"nonce":"xe3jzYUla3MuZzxgFw1j4qBeTHU=","title":"Dynamic item store released the key the dict kept","message":"`zb_any_setitem` declared its key parameter as a plain local while\n`zb_dict_set`, which it hands the key to when the receiver is a dict,\ndeclares it kept. The caller of the dynamic store therefore released a\nfreshly boxed key after the call, and the dict held a dangling box: its\nrepr printed an opaque box, and a second store into the same dict read\nfreed memory and faulted.\n\nReproducer: `d = 3; d = {}; d[(3, 8.0)] = \"p\"; d[(1, 2)] = \"q\"; print(d)`\n(the first assignment makes `d` dynamic, so the store goes through\n`zb_any_setitem`).\n\nFix: the dynamic store's key parameter is kept, as the dict's is.","files":null}]}